        "       Weighted avg (normalized) & 22.1 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 59.7 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 15.7 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 40.5 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 52.1 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 51.7 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0}\\\\\n",
        "       \\midrule\n",
        "       Weighted sum (unnormalized) & 59.9 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 92.2 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 38.2 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 76.2 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 76.2 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 83.5 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} \\\\\n",
        "       Weighted sum (normalized) & 74.1 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 99.3 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 48.0 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 86.8 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 80.7 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 88.7 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0}\\\\\n",
        "       \\midrule\n",
        "       Unweighted sum (majority vote) & 74.4 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.1} & 99.3 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.0} & 48.3 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.5} & 86.6 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.1} & 80.7 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.1} & 88.7 \\scriptsize{$\\pm$ 0.1} \\\\\n",
        "       \\bottomrule\n",
        "    \\end{tabular}\n",
        "    \\vspace{-0.1in}\n",
        "    \\label{tab:aggregation}\n",
        "\\vspace{-0.1in}\n",
        "\\end{table}\n",
        "Self-consistency explores an interesting space between open-ended text generation and optimal text generation with a fixed answer.\n",
        "Reasoning tasks typically have fixed answers, which is why researchers have generally considered greedy decoding approaches  \\citep{Radford2019LanguageMA,wei2022chain,palm}. \n",
        "One should note that self-consistency can be applied only to problems where the final answer is from a fixed answer set, but in principle this approach can be extended to open-text generation problems if a good metric of consistency can be defined between multiple generations, e.g., whether two answers agree or contradict each other.\n"
