            "We further study if self-consistency can help improve a language model's robustness to imperfect prompts.\\footnote{We use the same prompts as before, but swap all the numbers in the reasoning paths with random numbers except the final answer, e.g., from ``\\textit{There are 3 cars in the parking lot already. 2 more arrive. Now there are 3 + 2 = 5 cars.}'' to ``\\textit{There are \\textcolor{red}{7} cars in the parking lot already. \\textcolor{red}{6} more arrive. Now there are \\textcolor{red}{7 + 6} = 5 cars.}''.}\n",
